From 3f1389183ba2145eab89657373539daf016f3f82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:13:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 259/270] tegra_gr2d: bring-up driver for the 2D engine behind
 host1x

Reading /dev/misc/tegra_gr2d starts GR2D (PLL C / 2, 300 MHz), sends
command buffers through host1x channel 7 and waits for sync point 25,
then fills and copies rectangles in spare memory of the frame buffer
carveout and checks them, and times whole-surface fills and copies
against the CPU. Nothing is shown on the screen.

The channel DMA pointers DMAPUT, DMAGET and DMAEND are offsets from
DMASTART, and DMAINITGET copies DMAPUT into DMAGET: with absolute
pointers the DMA read from twice the address, which the memory
controller reported as a decode error of host1xdmar.

The command sequences follow grate (MIT). On a 512x300 32 bit surface
GR2D fills in 0.29 ms and copies in 0.68 ms; the CPU takes 0.78 ms
and 3.1 ms on the same write combining memory.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
